BEGIN_HYPERDESC
<h1>Destruction</h1>
Structural loads with the damage model on (the test sets ORBITER_DAMAGE=1):
Delta-gliders cruising, pulling up at full elevator and landing hard on
their gear keep all their parts; one spun up to 6 rad/s about its long
axis in orbit loses its wing tips; one dropped flat from 150 m breaks up
on the ground; one entering the atmosphere steeply at 11 km/s heats up
and fails; one below Jupiter's crush depth is crushed.
END_HYPERDESC

BEGIN_ENVIRONMENT
  System Sol
